  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Fast Maceo**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [4]\n- **Sea of Tranquility**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Au Privave**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Doin' Something**: back after 33 archived shows (544 days) [4]\n- **House Party**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Maceo Theme**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Aladdin, Elron, If You Want Me To Stay, Do It Again [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2003-02-05.dpa4022.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 13 songs; 141 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the recording's sound quality is great [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Set II [1]\n- Fred Wesley sang on one marked song, and Ivan Neville sang on another [1]\n- Jay Rodriguez played flute during the second set only; the Soulive Horn Section joined on some songs [1]\n- Reviewer describes hot jams and a band clearly having lots of fun [3]\n- Reviewer singles out Fred, cheering him on after revisiting the recording [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2003-02-05.dpa4022.shnf**: taped by Scott Brown; transferred by Scott Brown; source: DPA(B&K) 4022s > Lunatec V3 @ 16/44.1 > Sony D8 [1]. Also: Recorded with microphones clamped to the balcony, dead center, in an XY configuration [1]",
